cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research, please cite it as below."
title: "Sinhala Phonetic Orthography: a sourced rule set for Sinhala word construction and phonetic romanization"
authors:
  - family-names: Siriwardhana
    given-names: Srilal
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A sourced, consolidated rule set for how Sinhala words are written (88 rules over letter
  inventory, vowel signs, conjuncts, nasals, phonotactics and sandhi), a validity status for all
  923 Sinhala letter forms, measured evidence of how Sinhala is written and romanized from pinned
  public corpora, and a phonetic romanization whose reference converter is machine-checked never
  to produce a form the rules forbid.
repository-code: "https://github.com/SrilalS/sinhala-phonetic-orthography"
keywords:
  - Sinhala
  - orthography
  - phonetics
  - romanization
  - transliteration
  - Unicode
  - sandhi
